## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to derive nested-loop complexity where inner bound shrinks with i, revealing a harmonic-sum growth.

## Key Concepts
- Harmonic series: sum floor(n/i) ~ n log n
- Theta vs O, space O(1)
- Closed-form approximations vs exact sums

## Code Example
```javascript
function countPairs(n){
  let count=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let j=1;j<=Math.floor(n/i);j++){
      count++;
    }
  }
  return count;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you prove the Theta(n log n) bound?
- How does changing inner bound to floor(n/i^2) affect complexity?
- What are practical implications for large n?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to exploit DAG structure for incremental shortest paths with monotone updates and selective recomputation.

## Key Concepts
- DAG topological order
- Monotone updates and lazy propagation
- Selective relaxation focused on targets
- Amortized analysis of edge relaxations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for batch decreases
function applyDecreases(batch) {
  const queue = [];
  for (const e of batch) {
    if (dist[e.v] > dist[e.u] + e.newW) {
      dist[e.v] = dist[e.u] + e.newW;
      queue.push(e.v);
    }
  }
  queue.sort((a,b)=>topo[a]-topo[b]);
  while (queue.length) {
    const x = queue.shift();
    for (const y of adj[x]) {
      const w = weight(x,y);
      if (dist[y] > dist[x] + w) {
        dist[y] = dist[x] + w;
        queue.push(y);
      }
    }
  }
}
``` 

